{"thinking": "The F1 baseline on day 22 shows no line, so the 1.27 Hz line is tied to the bt-0431 period and is not a standing facility artefact. Evidence now leans toward training: there is a steady line during the run, outbound traffic stays flat while it runs, and a single ~40 TB export goes out on its last day. Against that, my own tap saw only inference-level traffic inside cluster A, and batch inference can also be periodic. The innocent reading predicts that Meridian Analytics is a real, independent customer that ordered batch inference and got its results in one delivery on day 19. The guilty reading predicts a shell or operator-linked customer, or one whose stated work doesn't match. The company register is hard for the operator to arrange, so customer_check on Meridian (cost 2, 16 points left after) is the next discriminator. After that: interconnect_tap on the A-B link or another event day, to look for traffic outside the intra-A links, and bank_payments.", "action": "customer_check", "args": {"customer": "Meridian Analytics"}}
```
